</ul><h1>Pull It Apart</h1><p>What are Peelerz, exactly?</p>
<p>Well, just take a look at this video, and all will be revealed:</p>
<p><iframe allowfullscreen class="youtube" frameborder="0" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/w9ABMl70E60?autohide=1&color=white&showinfo=0&theme=light"></iframe></p>
<p>Except, actually, their most unique feature, and the reason they’re called ‘Peelerz,’ is hidden in this little bit here:</p>
<p><img height="202" src="https://d2b8wt72ktn9a2.cloudfront.net/mediocre/image/upload/v1781531402/yblaito8xir4jtmnixuk.gif" width="360" /></p>
<p>They’re gummies… that you can peel! Weird, huh? But at least the peeling looks super easy.</p>
<p>Right?</p>
<p>Maybe. Maybe not.</p>
<p>In <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SRJD1Jf1YYc&t=49s">a review comparing Peelerz to a store-brand knock-off</a>, YouTuber Emmymade documented the process.</p>
<p>The beginning was a bit tough.</p>
<p><img height="202" src="https://d2b8wt72ktn9a2.cloudfront.net/mediocre/image/upload/v1781531595/n3aotygaxopygc0ftbzu.gif" width="360" /></p>
<p>But progress was ultimately made.</p>
<p><img height="202" src="https://d2b8wt72ktn9a2.cloudfront.net/mediocre/image/upload/v1781531630/smry0e7vprkvhntsrwja.gif" width="360" /></p>
<p>And eventually the center was revealed.</p>
<p><img height="202" src="https://d2b8wt72ktn9a2.cloudfront.net/mediocre/image/upload/v1781531648/kkpt6blkielxbxmgfv07.gif" width="360" /></p>
<p>Of course, the natural question to ask while watching this is… why? As in: why make gummies you can peel? But while I can’t say exactly what the brand was thinking, I see the appeal in a weird way. I was one of those kids who loved getting glue on their fingers and then pulling it off. And when I have peanut-butter-filled pretzels, I like to shuck them like an oyster, eat the peanut butter center, and then munch on the pretzel shell.</p>
<p>But if you’re not into food you can play with, just know: you can always just eat these whole.</p>